; fas9_assoc_history_surf.scr - facit script of step 9.15 (F9.11, Opus): the history entries of kind 8 (SURFTRIM) and kind 10
; (SURFFILLET) in the persistent subentity manager, in more forms than fas9_assoc_extended.scr and fas9_surfaces.scr have.
; Run it with
;   python -I tools/fas9_facit_run.py doc/facit/fas9_assoc_history_surf.scr
; It starts from AutoCAD's own acad.dwt (a new empty drawing) and uses plain AutoCAD commands, no LISP (the core has none).
; Every operation is drawn in a cell of its own, so a pick finds one object. Files: acad_<ver>_dxf_history_surf[_bin].dxf.
;
; SURFTRIM (top view, planes at z = 0):
;   T1  two planes side by side trimmed by one circle that crosses both (two surfaces in one trim)
;   T2  a plane cut in two by a line that crosses it, one side trimmed away
;   T3  a plane trimmed by a vertical surface that crosses it (a surface as the cutting edge)
;   T4  a plane trimmed by two circles in one trim (two cutting curves, two areas)
;   T5  two crossing vertical walls, each trimmed by the other in one trim
; SURFFILLET (south-west isometric view):
;   F1  two extruded walls at a right angle, radius 5 (as fas9_assoc_extended.scr)
;   F2  two walls, radius 3, Trim surface No
;   F3  a horizontal plane and a vertical wall standing on its edge, radius 4
;   F4  a plane and a wall extruded from a two-segment polyline (one surface of two faces), radius 2
;   F5  two walls at an oblique angle, radius 6
;EXPECT ACDBASSOCPERSSUBENTMANAGER
